 \265m\), which restricts the inter-chip communication to global metal lines. ) Tj24 -12  TD 0.0119  Tc 2.1481  Tw (One picture that strongly emerges from these futuristic devices is that the line) Tj-24 -12  TD 0.0121  Tc 0.8118  Tw (between chip, substrate, package, and board is blurring, and that designers of these sys-) Tj0 -12  TD 0.0172  Tc -0.0472  Tw (tems-on-a-die will have to consider all these aspects simultaneously.) Tj-36 -36  TD /F0 9.96  Tf-0.015  Tc 0  Tw (2.) Tj10.02  Tc (6) Tj0.027  Tc (Summary) Tj36 -24  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0235  Tc 0.0065  Tw (This chapter ) Tj52.32 0  TD 0.0167  Tc 0.0533  Tw (has presented an ) Tj68.88 0  TD 0.0178  Tc 0  Tw (a) Tj4.44 0  TD 0.0126  Tc 0.0924  Tw ( birds-eye view on issues regarding the manufacturing and) Tj-125.64 -12  TD 0.0088  Tc 0.0212  Tw (packaging of CMOS integrated circuits.) Tj12 -18  TD -0.006  Tc 0  Tw (\225) Tj12 0  TD 0.0176  Tc 1.136  Tw (The manufacturing process of integrated circuits require a large number of steps,) Tj0 -12  TD 0.0152  Tc 0.6662  Tw (each of which consists of a sequence of basic operations. A number of these steps) TjT* 0.0141  Tc 1.1259  Tw (and/or operations, such as photolithograpical exposure and development, material) TjT* 0.0131  Tc 0.0169  Tw (deposition, and etching, are executed very repetitively in the course of the manufac-) TjT* 0  Tc 0.0296  Tw (turing process.) TjET0.9686 0.9686 0.9686 rg 126.84 437.76 126.24 156.84 re f0 0 0 rg 126.84 594.12 126.72 0.96 re f252.6 437.28 0.96 157.32 re f126.36 437.28 126.72 0.96 re f126.36 437.76 0.96 157.32 re f0.702 0.702 0.702 rg 126.84 437.76 126.24 20.04 re f0 0 0 rg 126.84 457.56 126.48 0.48 re f252.84 437.52 0.48 20.28 re f126.6 437.52 126.48 0.48 re f126.6 437.76 0.48 20.28 re f0.502 0.502 0.502 rg 126.84 475.8 82.92 7.08 re f0 0 0 rg 126.84 482.64 83.16 0.48 re f209.52 475.56 0.48 7.32 re f126.6 475.56 83.16 0.48 re f126.6 475.8 0.48 7.32 re f0.502 0.502 0.502 rg 218.52 475.8 34.2