rge pin counts hence require extra routing layers to connect to the multitudes) TjT* 0.0099  Tc 1.0816  Tw (of pins. Finally, while the parasitic capacitance and inductance of the PGA are slightly) TjT* 0.0172  Tc -0.0199  Tw (lower than that of the DIP, their values are still substantial. ) Tj24 -12  TD 0.0159  Tc 1.2941  Tw (Many of the shortcomings of the through-hole mounting are solved by using the) Tj-24 -12  TD /F3 9.96  Tf0.0232  Tc 0  Tw (surface-mount) Tj57.72 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0113  Tc 0.1707  Tw ( technique. A chip is attached to the surface of the board with a solder con-) Tj-57.72 -12  TD 0.0159  Tc 0.5061  Tw (nection without requiring any through-holes \(Figure 2.14b\). Packing density is increased) Tj0 -12  TD 0.0184  Tc 0.6334  Tw (for the following reasons: \(1\) through-holes are eliminated, which provides more wiring) TjT* 0.0153  Tc 1.0029  Tw (space; \(2\) the lead pitch is reduced; and \(3\) chips can be mounted on both sides of the) TjT* 0.0144  Tc 0.2338  Tw (board. In addition, the elimination of the through-holes improves the mechanical strength) TjT* 0.0116  Tc 1.0484  Tw (of the board. On the negative side, the on-the-surface connection makes the chip-board) TjT* 0.0151  Tc 0.0229  Tw (connection weaker. Not only is it cumbersome to mount a component on a board, but also) TjT* 0.0114  Tc 0.5262  Tw (more expensive equipment is needed, since a simple soldering iron will not do anymore) Tj357.48 0  TD /F4 9.96  Tf0.03  Tc 0  Tw (.) Tj-357.48 -12  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0081  Tc 1.4019  Tw (Finally, testing of the board is more complex, because the package pins are no longer) Tj0 -12  TD 0.011  Tc 0.019  Tw (accessible at the backside of the board. Signal probing becomes hard or even impossible.) Tj24 -12  TD 0.0165  Tc 1.0035  Tw (A variety of surface-mount packages are currently in use with different pitch and) Tj-24 -12  TD 0.014  Tc -0.064  Tw (pin-count parameters. Three of these packages are shown in Figure 2.15: the ) Tj307.2 0  TD /F3 9.96  Tf0.0178  Tc 0  Tw (small-outline) Tj-307.2 -12  TD -0.0095  Tc (package) Tj33.24 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0128  Tc 0.1132  Tw ( with gull wings, the ) Tj85.08 0  TD /F3 9.96  Tf0.0108  Tc 0.0992  Tw (plastic leaded package ) Tj94.44 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0142  Tc 0.1358  Tw (\(PLCC\) with J-shaped leads, and the) TjET1 1 1 rg 381 571.2 118.92 18 re fBT381 583.92  TD0 0 0 rg /F0 7.92  Tf0.0303  Tc 0.0297  Tw (Figure 2.13) Tj46.56 0  TD /F1 7.92  Tf0.0292  Tc 0.0308  Tw (Flip-chip bonding.) TjET0.902 0.902 0.902 rg 201.12 592.8 156.96 18.12 re f0 0 0 rg 201.12 610.68 157.2 0.48 re f357.84 592.56 0.48 18.36 re f200.88 592.56 157.2 0.48 re f200.88 592.8 0.48 18.36 re f0.498 0.498 0.498 rg 218.52 633 122.16 8.4 re f218.52 641.16 122.4 0.48 re f340.44 632.76 0.48 8.64 re f218.28 632.76 122.4 0.48 re f218.28 633 0.48 8.64 re f0 0 0 rg 201.12 609.6 42.84 8.52 re f201.12 617.88 43.08 0.48 re f243.72 609.36 0.48 8.76 re f200.88 609.36 43.08 0.48 re f200.88 609.6 0.48 8.76 re f314.64 610.32 42.84 8.4 re f314.64 618.48 43.08 0.48 re f357.24 610.08 0.48 8.64 re f314.4 610.08 43.08 0.48 re f314.4 610.32 0.48 8.64 re f1 1 1 rg 325.8 631.68 m 325.08 631.68 l 323.88 631.44 l 322.68 630.96 l 321.72 630.24 l 321.24 629.76 l 320.76 629.4 l 320.4 628.8 l 320.04 628.32 l 319.56 627.12 l 319.32 625.92 l 319.32 624.6 l 319.44 623.88 l 319.56 623.28 l 320.04 622.08 l 320.76 621.12 l 321.72 620.16 l 322.2 619.8 l 322.68 619.56 l 323.28 619.2 l 323.88 618.96 l 325.08 618.72 l 333.12 618.72 l 333.84 618.84 l 334.44 618.96 l 335.04 619.2 l 335.64 619.56 l 336.12 619.8 l 336.6 620.16 l 337.56 621.12 l 337.92 621.6 l 338.16 622.08 l 338.52 622.68 l 338.64 623.28 l 338.88 623.88 l 339 624.6 l 339 625.92 l 338.88 626.52 l 338.64 627.12 l 338.52 627.72 l 338.16 628.32 l 337.92 628.8 l 337.56 629.4 l 337.08 629.76 l 336.6 630.24 l 335.64 630.96 l 334.44 631.44 l 333.84 631.56 l 333.12 63