 use) TjT* 0.0111  Tc 1.9922  Tw (advanced CAD techniques, which allow for migration between compatible processes.) TjT* 0.0122  Tc 0.8578  Tw (Another approach is to use) Tj0  Tc 0.03  Tw ( ) Tj113.88 0  TD /F3 9.96  Tf0.0056  Tc 0.8644  Tw (scalable design) Tj62.76 0  TD 0  Tc 0.87  Tw ( rules) Tj23.4 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0087  Tc 0.8613  Tw (. The latter approach, made popular by) Tj-200.04 -12  TD 0.0178  Tc 0.6808  Tw (Mead and Conway [Mead80], defines all rules as a function of a single parameter, most) Tj0 -12  TD 0.0134  Tc -0.0434  Tw (often called ) Tj49.2 0  TD /F4 9.96  Tf0.052  Tc 0  Tw (l) Tj5.52 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0092  Tc -0.0767  Tw (. The rules are chosen so that a design is easily ported over a cross section of) Tj-54.72 -12  TD 0.0129  Tc 2.6571  Tw (industrial processes. Scaling of the minimum dimension is accomplished by simply) Tj0 -12  TD 0.0159  Tc -0.0759  Tw (changing the value of ) Tj88.44 0  TD /F4 9.96  Tf0.052  Tc 0  Tw (l) Tj5.52 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0203  Tc -0.0863  Tw (. This results in a ) Tj70.56 0  TD /F3 9.96  Tf0.0178  Tc -0.1078  Tw (linear scaling) Tj55.08 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0129  Tc -0.1029  Tw ( of all dimensions. For a given pro-) Tj-219.6 -12  TD -0  Tc -0.0893  Tw (cess, ) Tj21.48 0  TD /F4 9.96  Tf-0.068  Tc -0.022  Tw (l ) Tj7.8 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0106  Tc -0.1744  Tw (is set to a specific value, and all design dimensions are consequently translated into) Tj-29.28 -12  TD 0.0173  Tc 2.1173  Tw (absolute numbers. Typically, the minimum line width of a process is set to ) Tj2.1  Tc 0  Tw (2) Tj333.48 0  TD /F4 9.96  Tf0.052  Tc (l) Tj5.52 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf-0.0011  Tc 2.0711  Tw (. For) Tj-339 -12  TD 0.0168  Tc 0.1332  Tw (instance, for a 0.25 ) Tj79.56 0  TD /F4 9.96  Tf0.023  Tc 0  Tw (m) Tj5.76 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0188  Tc 0.1512  Tw (m process \(i.e., a process with a minimum line width of 0.25 ) Tj247.2 0  TD /F4 9.96  Tf0.023  Tc 0  Tw (m) Tj5.76 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0415  Tc -0.0115  Tw (m\), ) Tj16.2 0  TD /F4 9.96  Tf0.052  Tc 0  Tw (l) Tj-354.48 -12  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0238  Tc -0.0538  Tw (equals 0.125 ) Tj53.04 0  TD /F4 9.96  Tf0.023  Tc 0  Tw (m) Tj5.76 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf-0.0194  Tc 0.0494  Tw (m. ) Tj-34.8 -12  TD 0.0111  Tc 0.0189  Tw (This approach, while attractive, suffers from some disadvantages: ) Tj-11.04 -18  TD /F0 9.96  Tf0.045  Tc 0  Tw (1.) Tj11.04 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0154  Tc 1.4546  Tw (Linear scaling is only possible over a limited range of dimensions \(for instance,) Tj0 -12  TD 0.013  Tc 1.817  Tw (between 0.25) Tj0  Tc 0.03  Tw ( ) Tj59.4 0  TD /F4 9.96  Tf0.023  Tc 0  Tw (m) Tj5.76 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0199  Tc 1.8101  Tw (m and 0.18) Tj0  Tc 0.03  Tw ( ) Tj52.68 0  TD /F4 9.96  Tf0.023  Tc 0  Tw (m) Tj5.76 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0111  Tc 1.836  Tw (m\). When scaling over larger ranges, the relations) Tj-123.6 -12  TD 0.0143  Tc 1.3957  Tw (between the different layers tend to vary in a nonlinear way that cannot be ade-) Tj0 -12  TD 0.0136  Tc -0.0236  Tw (quately covered by the linear scaling rules.) Tj-11.04 -18  TD /F0 9.96  Tf0.045  Tc 0  Tw (2.) Tj11.04 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.011  Tc 0.009  Tw (Scalable design rules are conservative. As they represent a cross section over differ-) Tj0 -12  TD 0.016  Tc 0.2817  Tw (ent technologies, they have to represent the worst-case rules for the whole set. This) TjT* 0.0121  Tc 0.0179  Tw (results in over-dimensioned and less-dense designs. ) Tj-24 -18  TD 0.0139  Tc -0.0319  Tw (For these reasons, scalable design rules are normally avoided by industry.) Tj294.6 4.08  TD /F1 6.96  Tf0  Tc 0  Tw (2) Tj3.6 -4.08  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0114  Tc -0.0214  Tw ( As circuit den-) Tj-298.2 -12  TD 0.0137  Tc 1.8532  Tw (sity is a prime goal in industrial designs, most semiconductor companies tend to use) Tj0 -12  TD /F3 9.96  Tf0.0094  Tc 1.3406  Tw (micron rules) Tj52.08 0  TD /F1 9.96  Tf0.0155  Tc 1.3345  Tw (, which express the design rul